        "format": "tilewright-adventure",
        "version": 7,
        "title": "The Keeper’s Loom",
        "author": "Lantern Trails",
        "description": "A program-stamp adventure: one opening rewrite, changing loops, ordered letters and shared crossings.",
        "intro": "The finale: four required stamps, three tube pairs, eight ordered flags and one keeper rewrite. Open your near wheel, then hold jade while Pip crosses. The route changes direction, operates its remote wheel, rings Pip’s bell and finishes on violet. Ring Home before crossing the signal gate. Pip must remain paused at the last address.",
        "ending": "The Loom begins to turn. Each window receives its letter, including the one beside your own little beacon. Inside your envelope are three blank cards. Pip has stamped one word on the back: “Together.”",
        "hint": "Turn the near wheel and step north onto jade. Apply East / East / Use, then advance twenty-five cards. The engraved route contains deliberate blocked moves beside the third tube and last stamp. Leave Pip on violet. Step south, walk east to the Home bell, ring it and bring the far light home.",
